      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "4. Section G: DialogKit Architecture & 37 Modal Dialogs"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1795702921463651700",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "M-28: DialogKit Canonical Primitives"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1795702921463652300",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "* **Implementation:** `crates/statcraft_app/src/dialogs/common/` (`dialog_shell.rs`, `action_bar.rs`, `subdialog_action_bar.rs`, `subdialog_sidebar.rs`, `variable_picker.rs`, `transfer_button.rs`, `group_box.rs`)\n* **SPSS Reference:** *SPSS Canonical Dialog Architecture & Ergonomics*\n* **Craft Anything Hypothesis:** `hyp_40` (Supported)\n* **Audited Invariants & Evidence:**\n  1. **Fixed Dialog Sizes (`DialogSize`):** Standard ($560 \\times 430$), Subdialog ($360 \\times 300$), Properties ($460 \\times 380$), Compute ($620 \\times 480$), Alert ($440 \\times 170$).\n  2. **Type 1 Action Bar (`DialogActionBar`):** Canonical sequence `[ OK ] [ Paste ] [ Reset ] [ Cancel ] [ Help ]`.\n  3. **i18n Shield:** Uniform button width auto-calculated across localized labels ($\\ge 80 \\times 26$ px, 3px rounding).\n  4. **Precondition Guard:** `[ OK ]` button automatically disables when procedural inputs are invalid.\n  5. **VariablePicker & TransferButton:** Vector measure icons (Scale, Ordinal, Nominal) and adaptive transfer buttons (`->` / `<-`)."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921463653900",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "M-29: Procedural Dialogs Suite (37 Dialogs, Subdialogs & Table Style)"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1795702921463654600",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "* **Implementation:** `crates/statcraft_app/src/dialogs/*.rs` (including `frequencies_dialog/format_subdialog.rs`, `charts_subdialog.rs`, `statistics_subdialog.rs`, `table_style_dialog/` (`mod.rs`, `state.rs`, `condition_subdialog.rs`, `format_subdialog.rs`), coordinator `app_dialogs.rs` and decomposed module `app_dialogs_stats.rs`)\n* **SPSS Reference:** *SPSS Procedural Dialogs Suite*\n* **Craft Anything Hypothesis:** `hyp_41` (Supported)\n* **Audited Invariants & Evidence:**\n  1. **Design Guard Linter (`cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- design-guard`):** 0 violations. Zero raw button calls, 100% DialogKit compliance.\n  2. **Subdialog Canonical Architecture:** Type 2 modal subdialogs (including *Frequencies: Statistics*, *Frequencies: Charts*, and *Frequencies: Format*, $360 \\times 300$ px) use `DialogShell::subdialog`, `GroupBox` and `SubdialogActionBar` (`[ Continue ] [ Cancel ] [ Help ]`) with rollback on cancel.\n     - *Frequencies: Format*: two-column selection of category ordering (`CategoryOrder` — 4 radio options), multi-variable organization (`MultipleVarsMode` — 2 radio options), checkbox and dependent threshold input for category table suppression `LIMIT(n)`;\n     - *Frequencies: Charts*: mutual exclusivity rules (Histogram vs Bar/Pie, normal curve gating).\n  3. **Table Style & Conditional Formatting Dialog Suite:**\n     - Main rules dialog `TableStyleDialog` ($640 \\times 420$ px): 5-column interactive rules grid (Enabled, Scope, Condition, Format, Delete), action buttons for rule addition, duplication, reordering (Up / Down), summary report generation toggle, and rule clearing.\n     - Condition subdialog `TableStyleConditionDialog` ($400 \\times 340$ px): dimension targeting (`Columns`, `Rows`, `Both`), 11 numeric comparison operators with single/interval inputs.\n     - Format subdialog `TableStyleFormatDialog` ($420 \\times 420$ px): typography (Bold, Italic), token palette swatches for text and background colors, interactive live preview sample box `SamplePreviewBox`.\n     - Transactionality: complete transactional snapshot mechanisms (`backup` / `cancel` / `confirm`) guaranteeing rollbacks on cancel across all subdialogs and the main dialog.\n     - Integration in `FrequenciesDialog` & `DescriptivesDialog`: activated `[ Style... ]` (`dialog-btn-style`) sidebar button, rule JSON serialization, and pipeline action dispatch.\n     - Canonical `DescriptivesDialog` (`crates/statcraft_app/src/dialogs/descriptives_dialog/`): decomposed into `mod.rs`, `state.rs`, and `options.rs`; includes `Save standardized values as variables` checkbox, `[ Style... ]` button, canonical `Descriptives: Options` subdialog ($440 \\times 390$ px with *Mean*, *Sum*, `GroupBox` *Dispersion*, *Distribution*, *Display Order*), and full `to_sps_full()` syntax generation on `Paste`.\n     - Reusable Bootstrap subdialog `BootstrapDialog` (`crates/statcraft_app/src/dialogs/bootstrap_dialog/`, $440 \\times 480$ px): built with `DialogShell`, `GroupBox` (*Confidence Intervals*, *Sampling*), `VariablePicker` + `TransferButton` for strata variables (enabled only under *Stratified*), `SubdialogActionBar`, transactional `backup`/`commit`/`cancel`, and activated `[ Bootstrap... ]` (`dialog-btn-bootstrap`) across 9 procedure dialogs (`FrequenciesDialog`, `DescriptivesDialog`, `MeansDialog`, `TTestOneSampleDialog`, `TTestIndepDialog`, `TTestPairedDialog`, `AnovaOnewayDialog`, `CorrelationsDialog`, `RegressionDialog`).\n  4. **Coordinator Architectural Decomposition (Rules 12.1 & 12.2 Anti-Goodhart):**\n     - Upon integrating `table_styles`, `crates/statcraft_app/src/app_dialogs.rs` reached 994 lines (approaching the 1000-line ceiling).\n     - In strict adherence to Rule 12.2 (\"Decompose, Never Cut\"), an architectural decomposition was conducted: the canonical SPSS Descriptive Statistics group (*Descriptives, Frequencies, Explore, Crosstabs*) was extracted into `crates/statcraft_app/src/app_dialogs_stats.rs` (284 lines).\n     - `