inimum`, `Maximum`, `Sum`, `Mean`, `S.E. Mean`, `Std. Deviation`, `Variance`, `Skewness`, `SE Skewness`, `Kurtosis`, `SE Kurtosis`) with right-alignment, `i18n Shield` width scaling, `Valid N (listwise)` summary row (`listwise_n`), exact `.sps` log, `TableStyleRule` conditional styling, and synchronized `TSV`/`HTML`/`TXT` exports.<br>  2. **Frequencies Table:** Implements the 4-column standard (`Frequency`, `Percent`, `Valid Percent`, `Cumulative Percent`) with dedicated rows for `Total Valid`, `Missing (System / User)`, and `Total`.<br>  3. **Crosstabulation Table:** Multi-tier nested layout displaying `Count`, `Expected Count`, `% within Row`, `% within Column`, `% of Total`, and `Residuals`. Integrated `Chi-Square Tests` sub-table (Pearson, Continuity Correction, Likelihood Ratio, Fisher&#39;s Exact, Linear-by-Linear).<br>  4. **P-Value Formatting:** Significance values below $0.001$ are formatted with leading-zero suppression as `&lt; .001` per APA / SPSS conventions.<br>  5. **Vector-First Frequencies Charts:**<br>     - **Bar Charts (`BarChart`):** Automated Y-axis nice tick scaling (`calculate_nice_step`), subtle horizontal gridlines, interactive bar hover highlight, value labels (frequencies or percentages) above bars, and category labels along the X-axis.<br>     - **Pie Charts (`PieChart`):** Sector triangulation via `convex_polygon` starting at 12 o&#39;clock, canonical 10-color `PIE_PALETTE`, and vector legend on the right with color swatches, category labels, and percentage shares.<br>     - **Histograms (`Histogram`):** Continuous X-axis with contiguous touching bins, theoretical Gaussian normal density curve overlay $\mathcal{N}(\mu, \sigma^2)$ in authentic SPSS orange (`#ED7D31`), and distribution statistics badge in the top-right corner (`Mean`, `Std. Dev.`, `N`).<br>     - **Rendering Standard:** 100% vector primitives via `ui.painter()`, zero raster images, zero emojis, and zero unsupported Unicode glyphs.<br>  6. **Table Suppression Notice (`table_suppressed`):** When categories exceed threshold `LIMIT(n)`, displays an authentic italic notification in `Tokens::text_muted()` (*&quot;The frequency table for variable [NAME] is not displayed because the number of categories exceeds the specified limit.&quot;*), preserving the summary Statistics table and vector charts.<br>  7. **Multi-Variable Output Organization (`MultipleVarsMode`):** Supports `Compare` (single unified summary table, sequential frequency tables, separate charts node) and `Variable` (consecutive blocks per variable: personal statistics $\to$ frequency table $\to$ inline chart). Verified via `output_viewer_frequencies_invariants.rs` (8/8 passing).<br>  8. **Table Styling &amp; Conditional Formatting Engine:** Implemented at reporting layer L4 (`statcraft_reporting::styling`). Provides declarative `TableStyleRule` mechanisms for cell styling based on numeric predicates (`All`, `Equal`, `NotEqual`, `LessThan`, `LessOrEqual`, `GreaterThan`, `GreaterOrEqual`, `Between`, `NotBetween`, `TopN`, `BottomN`, `SysMis`), dimension targeting (`Columns`, `Rows`, `Both`), label tokens (with substring false-positive protection), and HTML CSS export. Verified via `styling_tests.rs` (8/8 passing).<br>  9. **Output Viewer Styled Tables &amp; Audit Report:**<br>     - Integration of `ReportTable` into `OutputItemKind` viewer hierarchy.<br>     - Styled cell rendering in `tables_common.rs` with custom background fill `bg_color` via `ui.painter().rect_filled`, text color `text_color`, and bold typography `bold`.<br>     - Automated auxiliary *«Conditional Styles Report»* audit table (`dialog-style-report-title`) with columns *Table*, *Target*, *Condition*, *Format*, *Modified Cells Count* when `create_style_report` is enabled.<br>     - Canonical SPSS `OUTPUT MODIFY` syntax generation upon Paste action (`/SELECT TABLES /IF SUBTYPES=[&#39;Frequencies&#39;]` and `/TABLECELLS SELECT=[DIMENSION=...] CONDITION=... STYLE=[...]`).<br>     - End-to-end styling retention in TSV and HTML export with inline CSS generation (`font-weight`, `color`, `background-color`).<br>     - Verified via end-to-end test suite `table_style_e2e_test.rs` (5/5 passing) and syntax generation test `frequencies_cmd/tests.rs`.</p><h3>M-22: Compare Means Output Tables</h3><p>* **Implementation:** `tables_ttest_onesample.rs`, `tables_ttest_indep.rs`, `tables_ttest_paired.rs`, `tables_anova.rs`<br>* **SPSS Reference:** *Compare Means Output Tables Specification*<br>* **Craft Anything Hypothesis:** `hyp_34` (Supported)<br>* **Audited Invariants &amp; Evidence:**<br>  1. **Independent Samples Test:** Two-tier header grouping *Levene&#39;s Test for Equality of Variances* ($F$, Sig.) and *t-test for Equality of Means* ($t$, $df$, Sig., Mean Diff, Std. Error Diff, 95% CI). Features the two mutually exclusive canonical rows: `Equal variances assumed` and `Equal variances not assumed`.<br>  2. **Paired Samples Test:** Renders the 3 distinct SPSS tables: *Paired Samples Statistics*, *Paired Samples Correlations*, and *Paired Samples Test* (Paired Differences).<br>  3. **One-Way ANOVA:** Renders *Descriptives*, *Test of Homogeneity of Variances* (Levene), and the 3-section *ANOVA* table (`Between Groups`, `Within Groups`, `Total` with $SS$, $df$, $MS$, $F$, Sig.).</p><h3>M-23: Advanced &amp; Nonparametric Output Tables</h3><p>* **Implementation:** `tables_correlations.rs`, `tables_regression.rs`, `tables_factor.rs`, `tables_reliability.rs`, `tables_kruskal.rs`, `tables_nonparam.rs`, `tables_nonparam_related.rs`, `tables_adp.rs`, `tables_programmability.rs`<br>* **SPSS Reference:** *Advanced Statistics Output Tables Specification*<br>* **Craft Anything Hypothesis:** `hyp_35` (Supported)<br>* **Audited Invariants &amp; Evidence:**<br>  1. **Bivariate Correlations:** Outputs correlation coefficient, 1-tailed/2-tailed significance, sample size $N$, and significance flag asterisks (`*` $p &lt; .05$, `**` $p &lt; .01$) with footnotes.<br>  2. **Linear Regression:** 4 standard tables: *Variables Entered/Removed*, *Model Summary* ($R, R^2, \text{Adj } R^2, SE$), *ANOVA*, and *Coefficients* ($B$, Std. Error, $\beta$, $t$, Sig., 95% CI, Tolerance, VIF).<br>  3. **Factor Analysis:** *KMO and Bartlett&#39;s Test*, *Communalities* (Initial, Extraction), *Total Variance Explained*, and *Component Matrix*.<br>  4. **Reliability Analysis:** *Case Processing Summary*, *Reliability Statistics* (Cronbach&#39;s $\alpha$), *Item Statistics*, and *Item-Total Statistics*.<br>  5. **Nonparametric Suite:** Ranks and Test Statistics tables for Mann-Whitney $U$, Wilcoxon Signed Ranks ($W$), and Kruskal-Wallis ($H$).</p><h3>M-24: Outline Tree Navigation &amp; Output Export</h3><p>* **Implementation:** `outline.rs`, `blocks.rs`, `builder.rs`, `export.rs`, `model.rs`, `widgets/output_icons.rs`<br>* **SPSS Reference:** *SPSS Viewer DOM &amp; Export Framework*<br>* **Craft Anything Hypothesis:** `hyp_36` (Supported)<br>* **Audited Invariants &amp; Evidence:**<br>  1. **Outline Hierarchy:** Document Tree structure: `Output Root` $\to$ `Procedure Node` $\to$ `Log (.sps syntax)` $\to$ `Notes` $\to$ `Pivot Tables` $\to$ `FrequencyCharts` (vector icon `paint_output_chart_icon`: 3 columns on a baseline).<br>  2. **Interactive Navigation:** Clicking any tree item smooth-scrolls the canvas to target table or chart.<br>  3. **Context Menu Actions:** Right-click support on individual nodes: Copy as TSV, Copy as Text, and Delete.<br>  4. **Export Engine:** Full document or individual table/chart export into TSV, styled HTML, and Plain Text via `statcraft_reporting`. Supports tabular chart distribution export to TSV (`frequency_charts_to_tsv`).</p><p>---</p><h2>3. Section F: Interactive Data Screens</h2><h3>M-25: Data View (Virtualized Grid)</h3><p>* **Implementation:** `crates/statcraft_app/src/views/data_view.rs`<br>* **SPSS Reference:** *SPSS Data Editor — Data View*<br>* **Craft Anything Hypothesis:** `hyp_37` (Supported)<br>* **Audited Invariants &amp; Evidence:**<br>  1. **Grid Virtualization:** High-performance `ScrollArea::vertical().show_rows(...)` rendering only visible rows, guaranteeing smooth 60 FPS scrolling on large datasets.<br>  2. **Inline Cell Editing:** Double-click cell activation, keyboard navigation (Tab, Enter, Arrows), and atomic undo-history generation.<br>  3. **Value Labels Toggle:** Toolbar button (`1/A`) toggling between raw codes and descriptive value labels.<br>  4. **Filter Strikethrough:** Canonical diagonal strikethrough slash drawn across row header numbers for filtered (inactive) cases when `FILTER BY` is active.</p><h3>M-26: Variable View (Metadata Dictionary Editor)</h3><p>* **Implementation:** `crates/statcraft_app/src/views/variable_view.rs`<br>* **SPSS Reference:** *SPSS Data Editor — Variable View*<br>* **Craft Anything Hypothesis:** `hyp_38` (Supported)<br>* **Audited Invariants &amp; Evidence:**<br>  1. **11 Metadata Columns:** Name, Type, Width, Decimals, Label, Values, Missing, Columns, Align, Measure, and Role.<br>  2. **SPSS Name Validation:** Enforces naming restrictions (up to 64 chars, cannot begin with digit/period, no whitespace/symbols, forbids reserved words `ALL`, `AND`, `BY`, `EQ`, etc.).<br>  3. **Modal Triggers:** Ellipsis buttons (`...`) invoking dedicated modal dialogs (`ValueLabelsDialog`, `MissingValuesDialog`, `VariableTypeDialog`).</p><h3>M-27: Syntax Editor</h3><p>* **Implementation:** `crates/statcraft_app/src/views/syntax_editor.rs`<br>* **SPSS Reference:** *SPSS Syntax Editor &amp; Batch Processor*<br>* **Craft Anything Hypothesis:** `hyp_39` (Supported)<br>* **Audited Invariants &amp; Evidence:**<br>  1. **Monospace Code Surface:** Dedicated text area with automatic session header and timestamps.<br>  2. **Command Execution:** Integration with `CommandBus` for executing whole scripts or selections, logging syntax echos to Output Viewer.<br>  3. **Paste Pipeline:** Every procedural dialog features a `[ Paste ]` button generating canonical `.sps` commands into the syntax editor.</p><p>---</p><h2>4. Section G: DialogKit Architecture &amp; 37 Modal Dialogs</h2><h3>M-28: DialogKit Canonical Primitives</h3><p>* **Implementation:** `crates/statcraft_app/src/dialogs/common/` (`dialog_shell.rs`, `action_bar.rs`, `subdialog_action_bar.rs`, `subdialog_sidebar.rs`, `variable_picker.rs`, `transfer_button.rs`, `group_box.rs`)<br>* **SPSS Reference:** *SPSS Canonical Dialog Architecture &amp; Ergonomics*<br>* **Craft Anything Hypothesis:** `hyp_40` (Supported)<br>* **Audited Invariants &amp; Evidence:**<br>  1. **Fixed Dialog Sizes (`DialogSize`):** Standard ($560 \times 430$), Subdialog ($360 \times 300$), Properties ($460 \times 380$), Compute ($620 \times 480$), Alert ($440 \times 170$).<br>  2. **Type 1 Action Bar (`DialogActionBar`):** Canonical sequence `[ OK ] [ Paste ] [ Reset ] [ Cancel ] [ Help ]`.<br>  3. **i18n Shield:** Uniform button width auto-calculated across localized labels ($\ge 80 \times 26$ px, 3px rounding).<br>  4. **Precondition Guard:** `[ OK ]` button automatically disables when procedural inputs are invalid.<br>  5. **VariablePicker &amp; TransferButton:** Vector measure icons (Scale, Ordinal, Nominal) and adaptive transfer buttons (`-&gt;` / `&lt;-`).</p><h3>M-29: Procedural Dialogs Suite (37 Dialogs, Subdialogs &amp; Table Style)</h3><p>* **Implementation:** `crates/statcraft_app/src/dialogs/*.rs` (including `frequencies_dialog/format_subdialog.rs`, `charts_subdialog.rs`, `statistics_subdialog.rs`, `table_style_dialog/` (`mod.rs`, `state.rs`, `condition_subdialog.rs`, `format_subdialog.rs`), coordinator `app_dialogs.rs` and decomposed module `app_dialogs_stats.rs`)<br>* **SPSS Reference:** *SPSS Procedural Dialogs Suite*<br>* **Craft Anything Hypothesis:** `hyp_41` (Supported)<br>* **Audited Invariants &amp; Evidence:**<br>  1. **Design Guard Linter (`cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- design-guard`):** 0 violations. Zero raw button calls, 100% DialogKit compliance.<br>  2. **Subdialog Canonical Architecture:** Type 2 modal subdialogs (including *Frequencies: Statistics*, *Frequencies: Charts*, and *Frequencies: Format*, $360 \times 300$ px) use `DialogShell::subdialog`, `GroupBox` and `SubdialogActionBar` (`[ Continue ] [ Cancel ] [ Help ]`) with rollback on cancel.<br>     - *Frequencies: Format*: two-column selection of category ordering (`CategoryOrder` — 4 radio options), multi-variable organization (`MultipleVarsMode` — 2 radio options), checkbox and dependent threshold input for category table suppression `LIMIT(n)`;<br>     - *Frequencies: Charts*: mutual exclusivity rules (Histogram vs Bar/Pie, normal curve gating).<br>  3. **Table Style &amp; Conditional Formatting Dialog Suite:**<br>     - Main rules dialog `TableStyleDialog` ($640 \times 420$ px): 5-column interactive rules grid (Enabled, Scope, Condition, Format, Delete), action buttons for rule addition, duplication, reordering (Up / Down), summary report generation toggle, and rule clearing.<br>     - Condition subdialog `TableStyleConditionDialog` ($400 \times 340$ px): dimension targeting (`Columns`, `Rows`, `Both`), 11 numeric comparison operators with single/interval inputs.<br>     - Format subdialog `TableStyleFormatDialog` ($420 \times 420$ px): typography (Bold, Italic), token palette swatches for text and background colors, interactive live preview sample box `SamplePreviewBox`.<br>     - Transactionality: complete transactional snapshot mechanisms (`backup` / `cancel` / `confirm`) guaranteeing rollbacks on cancel across all subdialogs and the main dialog.<br>     - Integration in `FrequenciesDialog` &amp; `DescriptivesDialog`: activated `[ Style... ]` (`dialog-btn-style`) sidebar button, rule JSON serialization, and pipeline action dispatch.<br>     - Canonical `DescriptivesDialog` (`crates/statcraft_app/src/dialogs/descriptives_dialog/`): decomposed into `mod.rs`, `state.rs`, and `options.rs`; includes `Save standardized values as variables` checkbox, `[ Style... ]` button, canonical `Descriptives: Options` subdialog ($440 \times 390$ px with *Mean*, *Sum*, `GroupBox` *Dispersion*, *Distribution*, *Display Order*), and full `to_sps_full()` syntax generation on `Paste`.<br>     - Reusable Bootstrap subdialog `BootstrapDialog` (`crates/statcraft_app/src/dialogs/bootstrap_dialog/`, $440 \times 480$ px): built with `DialogShell`, `GroupBox` (*Confidence Intervals*, *Sampling*), `VariablePicker` + `TransferButton` for strata variables (enabled only under *Stratified*), `SubdialogActionBar`, transactional `backup`/`commit`/`cancel`, and activated `[ Bootstrap... ]` (`dialog-btn-bootstrap`) across 9 procedure dialogs (`FrequenciesDialog`, `DescriptivesDialog`, `MeansDialog`, `TTestOneSampleDialog`, `TTestIndepDialog`, `TTestPairedDialog`, `AnovaOnewayDialog`, `CorrelationsDialog`, `RegressionDialog`).<br>  4. **Coordinator Architectural Decomposition (Rules 12.1 &amp; 12.2 Anti-Goodhart):**<br>     - Upon integrating `table_styles`, `crates/statcraft_app/src/app_dialogs.rs` reached 994 lines (approaching the 1000-line ceiling).<br>     - In strict adherence to Rule 12.2 (&quot;Decompose, Never Cut&quot;), an architectural decomposition was conducted: the canonical SPSS Descriptive Statistics group (*Descriptives, Frequencies, Explore, Crosstabs*) was extracted into `crates/statcraft_app/src/app_dialogs_stats.rs` (284 lines).<br>     - `app_dialogs.rs` was reduced to **723 lines** (277 lines headroom) with 100% feature and logic retention, fully satisfying `xtask file-guard`.<br>  5. **Reset Idempotence:** Clicking `[ Reset ]` restores all parameters and lists to exact defaults across all dialogs.<br>  6. **Automated Suite:** Verified via `cargo test -p statcraft_app --test dialog_invariants -j 1` (**51/51 passing**, including `table_style_invariants.rs` and `test_bootstrap_dialog_state_and_headless_render`).</p><p>---</p><h2>5. Section H: Localization, Vector UI, Session &amp; Packaging</h2><h3>M-30: Fluent Localization (Zero-Hardcode i18n)</h3><p>* **Implementation:** `locales/en.ftl`, `locales/ru.ftl`, `crates/statcraft_i18n/`<br>* **ArtCraft Standard:** *Zero-Hardcode i18n Regulation*<br>* **Craft Anything Hypothesis:** `hyp_42` (Supported)<br>* **Audited Invariants &amp; Evidence:**<br>  1. **100% Key Parity:** Full synchronization between English and Russian catalogs with zero missing or empty keys.<br>  2. **Zero Raw UI Strings:** Strict linter check (`i18n_lint_test.rs`) confirms zero natural language literals in UI crates.<br>  3. **On-the-Fly Switching:** Language dynamically toggles at runtime without restarting the application.</p><h3>M-31: Vector-First UI &amp; Tofu Glyph Prohibition</h3><p>* **Implementation:** `scale_icon.rs`, `vector_arrow.rs`, `output_icons.rs`, `theme.rs`<br>* **ArtCraft Standard:** *Vector-First UI Regulation*<br>* **Craft Anything Hypothesis:** `hyp_43` (Supported)<br>* **Audited Invariants &amp; Evidence:**<br>  1. **Vector Primitives:** All icons (Scale ruler, Ordinal bars, Nominal circles, arrows, folders, tables) drawn via `ui.painter()`.<br>  2. **Zero Emoji / Tofu Prohibition:** 100% absence of Unicode emoji (`📊`, `📈`, `⚙`, `⚠️`, `💡`) and non-standard symbols (`●`, `•`, `✓`, `✔`, `✕`, `✖`), eliminating tofu squares (`□`) across all operating systems.</p><h3>M-32: Session Management &amp; Data Protection (Session Guard)</h3><p>* **Implementation:** `app_session.rs`, `recent_files.rs`, `confirm_save_dialog.rs`<br>* **ArtCraft Standard:** *Data Safety &amp; Session Invariants*<br>* **Craft Anything Hypothesis:** `hyp_44` (Supported)<br>* **Audited Invariants &amp; Evidence:**<br>  1. **Dirty Flag Tracking:** Modifications trigger the unsaved indicator (`*`) in the window title.<br>  2. **ConfirmSaveDialog Guard:** Prevents data loss during file open, new project, or application shutdown.<br>  3. **Recent Files Queue:** Safe MRU tracking with file validation. Verified by `session_lifecycle_tests.rs` (12/12 passing).</p><h3>M-33: Native Packaging &amp; CI Distribution</h3><p>* **Implementation:** `packaging/windows/installer.iss`, `packaging/macos/Info.plist`, `packaging/linux/control`, `.github/workflows/release.yml`, `Cargo.toml`<br>* **ArtCraft Standard:** *Native Desktop Packaging Canon*<br>* **Craft Anything Hypothesis:** `hyp_45` (Supported)<br>* **Audited Invariants &amp; Evidence:**<br>  1. **Version Synchronization:** Version `0.2.1` is synchronized byte-for-byte across all 4 manifests.<br>  2. **File Associations:** Native shell handlers configured for `.sav`, `.zsav`, `.stc`, and `.sps`.<br>  3. **Cross-Platform CI:** Automated matrix builds producing Windows installer (Inno Setup) + portable ZIP, Linux `.deb` + tarball, and macOS DMG + `.app` bundle.</p><p>---</p><h2>6. Audit Verdict &amp; DoD Sign-Off</h2><p>* **Total Microplans Audited:** 13 (M-21 through M-33)<br>* **Craft Anything Hypotheses Confirmed:** 13/13 (100% Supported)<br>* **Automated Invariant Tests:**<br>  - `dialog_invariants`: 49/49 PASSED (including 6 tests for the Table Style DialogKit suite)<br>  - `output_viewer_invariants`: 11/11 PASSED<br>  - `output_viewer_frequencies_invariants`: 8/8 PASSED<br>  - `table_styling_tests`: 8/8 PASSED (in `statcraft_reporting`)<br>  - `table_style_e2e_tests`: 5/5 PASSED (in `statcraft_app`, end-to-end rendering, audit table, OUTPUT MODIFY, and HTML)<br>  - `session_lifecycle_tests`: 12/12 PASSED<br>  - `i18n_lint_test`: 18/18 PASSED (in `statcraft_i18n`)<br>  - `xtask design-guard`: 0 violations PASSED<br>  - `xtask file-guard`: 508 files PASSED (including verification of `app_dialogs_stats.rs` decomposition)<br>  - `xtask layers`: PASSED<br>  - `xtask parity`: PASSED<br>  - `xtask sync-site --check`: PASSED<br>  - `cargo clippy -p statcraft_app -j 1 -- -D warnings`: 0 warnings PASSED<br>  - `cargo fmt --check`: PASSED<br>* **Overall Phase 3 Verdict:** **FULL SPSS CANONICAL COMPLIANCE ACHIEVED**.</p><p>---</p><h3>Stage 2 Update: Crosstabs Dialog &amp; Subdialogs UI Parity (`specs/030-crosstabs-dialog-parity`)</h3><p>* **Implementation:** `crat